ATE_PEAK_RSS convention but does not state whether/how a ticket id reaches gate_admission","gate_admission 'sits strictly OUTSIDE' gate_peak_rss and 'wraps handle resolution AND the run'"],"finding":"AC7 requires the GATE_CONGESTED marker to name 'gate, ticket and limit', but the plan never establishes that a ticket identifier is in scope at the gate_admission seam (which wraps handle resolution + the run, outside gate_peak_rss). The provenance of the 'ticket' field in the marker is unstated.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f683ed3bb459955b3","impact":0.44,"is_primary":null,"location":"AC7 / Design 'Metric (AC7)'","norm_id":"n4a08fee8c739b425","priority":0.11,"reason":"veto:absence-refuted","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Executor implements the marker but has no ticket id available at the admission seam and must guess the source or stop to ask"],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"Name the parameter that supplies the ticket id to gate_admission, matching the field already emitted by GATE_PEAK_RSS.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.25,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"no","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"no","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"no","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"underspecified_oracle","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"none","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"none","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"low"}}},{"block_threshold":0.95,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Specify the counter's acquisition algorithm (open/try-flock each of the N slot paths, admit on first LOCK_NB success, refuse when all N hold) and when the N slot files are created (create-on-open vs pre-seeded).","cohort":["E3","E5","G5","T5b","T6","T9","necessity","project.failure-disposition-contract","project.portability"],"criteria":["T9"],"decision":"dropped","decision_margin":-0.884,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["'N slot files in the store's existing locks/ dir, each held for the run under a non-blocking fcntl.flock(LOCK_EX|LOCK_NB), released in a finally.'","The CREATE and atomic-acquisition legs of the lifecycle are load-bearing for AC1 (one counter bounds both gates) and AC4 (cross-process bound) but the plan gives no acquisition loop or file-creation timing."],"finding":"The counter's slot-acquisition and slot-file creation semantics are under-specified: the plan says N slot files are each held under a non-blocking flock but never states the acquisition algorithm (iterate the N slot paths, admit on the first flock that succeeds, refuse only when all N are held) nor who creates the slot files and when (created on first open, or pre-seeded).","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f1403444f89bd69d3","impact":0.264,"is_primary":null,"location":"Design — 'Counter.'","norm_id":"n0dfb41f1bf6da728","priority":0.066,"reason":"low-validity","recalled":false,"scenarios":["An implementer could open a single fixed slot file (serialising to 1) or race on file creation, silently diverging from the intended cap of N."],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"State: 'slot_0..slot_{N-1} are opened (O_CREAT) and flock(LOCK_EX|LOCK_NB) tried in order; admission wins on the first success and holds that FD for the run; if all N fail, refuse.'","tier":"LLM","validity":0.25,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","com